From: Ken Hornstein <kenh@cmf.nrl.navy.mil>
To: jkatz@corinne.mac.edu
Date: Sat, 14 Jun 1997 11:37:16 +0000
Subject: Re: PPP and an ISA modem...

>I have an AXPpci33 motherboard up and running, and I even got
>PPP compiled into ther kernel! My problem is this: I'm having trouble
>getting the modem to work with isacfg-- I was able to disable the
>internal "Com2" but when I go to use isacfg to make the device in
>the SRM console, I get an "ISA Table is Full" error. Has anyone had
>any experience with this and gotten it to work? 

It turns out that the format of the isacfg table has changed between
firmware revisions.  If you use "isacfg -init" (or something similar)
it will reset the ISA device table and you'll be able to add stuff.

--Ken

